• Owning the roadmap and prioritization for your areas of Voice, balancing customer demand, scalability, reliability, and engineering dependencies &nbsp;

• Defining and evolving voice platform capabilities, including APIs and integrations, that let customers and partners extend and tailor voice experiences &nbsp;

• Driving a great customer and partner experience, from onboarding and documentation to self‑service configuration and time to value &nbsp;

• Integrating AI‑native capabilities, including conversational AI, generative AI, real‑time transcription, and agent assist, into voice experiences &nbsp;

• Contributing to packaging and pricing for Voice capabilities &nbsp;

• Defining requirements, user stories, and acceptance criteria, and driving features from discovery through GA and adoption &nbsp;

• Planning and executing against quarterly release trains, keeping status, documentation, and risks current and visible &nbsp;

• Defining and tracking outcome‑based KPIs such as feature adoption, usage and call volume, quality and reliability, and revenue impact &nbsp;

• Supporting enterprise sales opportunities, partner engagements, and high‑level customer escalations &nbsp;

• Partnering with product marketing on positioning, launch readiness, partner enablement, and release communications &nbsp;

• Monitoring competitive and market trends across cloud communications and contact center platforms to help NiCE stay ahead &nbsp;

